				\begin{document}$${\text{Swelling}}\;{\text{Ratio}} = \frac{{{\text{(W}}_{{{\text{final}}}} - {\text{W}}_{{{\text{initial}}}} {)}}}{{{\text{W}}_{{{\text{initial}}}} }}$$\end{document} Biodegradation test of scaffolds Scaffolds were given the exact dimensions and weighed. Then, the scaffold samples were incubated in a phosphate buffer solution for 21, 14, and 7 days at 37 °C with pH = 7.4. After the specified time, the samples were dried using the freeze-drying method and weighed. The scaffold destruction rate was obtained by the following equation 37 : 3 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
