g the freeze-drying method. Finally, EDX and SEM techniques were employed to evaluate the biomineralization capability of the scaffold samples 38 . Assessment of toxicity and cell viability First, uniform pieces of scaffolds were cut and immersed in 70% ethanol solution for 30 min to sterilize them. Eventually, we must continue using PBS to remove any remaining ethanol from the system and transfer it to a 96-well cell culture plate. Then, mesenchymal stem cells were cultured on the scaffolds with a cell density of 1 × 10 4  cells per cell plate. After collecting the samples, they were cultured inside the incubator in a DMEM medium containing 1% penicillin–streptomycin and 10% FBS. They were incubated for 72 h at 37 °C. After 72 h, the supernatant of all the wells of the 96-well plate was removed, and after washing with PBS to each well, 0.2 ml of MTT solution (5 mg/mm) was added, and the wells were kept in the incubator for four hours. It was incubated at 37 °C. A solution of 0.1 mL DMSO was then substituted for the MTT solution for 30 min. Finally, the absorbance was measured by an ELISA reader at a wavelength of 570 nm to determine cell viability.

